---
// The viewport as an instrument: the playhead, where you are in reading time.
// Drawn at the edges, never in the way: hidden from assistive tech, deaf to
// the pointer, and only alive when the script runs on an article. On a wide
// screen it is a timeline down the right edge; elsewhere, a top hairline.
---

<div class="playhead" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<div class="furniture" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="timeline"><div class="fill"></div><div class="head micro"><span class="time"></span></div></div>
</div>
